          "name": "pqs:context",
          "value": "AES-GCM is the session AEAD for every TLS connection in this app: TLS 1.3 AES-128/256-GCM suites plus TLS 1.2 ECDHE-RSA/ECDSA-AES-GCM fallback, provided by aws-lc-rs for the rustls/reqwest HTTPS path and by OpenSSL for the native-tls WSS path (ring's implementation ships via rustls-webpki/quinn-proto). Quantum-safe in the relevant sense: Grover halves key length, so AES-128 keeps a 64-bit quantum margin — CNSA 2.0 prefers AES-256 but this is not an emergency. No first-party call sites."
